### Topic 31 - Spring MVC & REST Fundamentals (Book API)
### Start the app first: mvn spring-boot:run
### Click "Send Request" above each request (VS Code "REST Client" extension).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/books

### 1. Get all books
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 2. Get one book by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/2

### 3. A book that does not exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/999

### 4. Search by author (query parameter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?author=bloch

### 5. Add a new book (JSON body) -> 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Java Concurrency in Practice",
  "author": "Brian Goetz",
  "year": 2006,
  "price": 800
}

### 6. Delete a book -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/3

### 7. Ask for the response headers too - look at Content-Type: application/json
GET {{baseUrl}}/1
Accept: application/json
